// VOLD_limit_depth.schema — OLD: the fixed form's nesting bound, AT the bound
//
// docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §3.4's fixed_max_depth is 64 (ir.TableFixedMaxDepth, every
// runtime's kTableFixedMaxDepth), and the root is depth 0. Here d is depth 1,
// the D<k> entry is depth k, and D63's v is the deepest entry at depth 64, so
// this layout nests exactly as deep as the bound allows; one level more and the
// compiler does not emit the fixed form. Each level's nested field comes first
// and a byte follows it: Go's type checker sizes a struct whose LAST field is a
// struct by sizing that field twice, so a chain of last fields costs 2^depth
// to compile, and this chain must compile in every leg.
// VOLD_limit_depth and VNEW_limit_depth differ by v's range alone (0..100, then
// 0..200): the layout bytes are the same and the hashes differ, so the NEW
// reader holds the OLD layout as a lineage entry and parses it under the bound
// when it builds its plan (docs/FIXED-FORM-ALGORITHM.md §1.1, §5).
// test/tables/fixedform_dump.cpp writes old_limit_depth.bin from the OLD unit
// and derives hostile_limit_depth.bin from it, the same file with one more
// table level spliced into its layout.

package vold_limit_depth

type D63
{
    v int32 = 0 | min = 0, max = 100
}

type D62
{
    d    D63
    tail uint8
}

type D61
{
    d    D62
    tail uint8
}

